WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:05.440
1999's The Mummy blew audiences away&nbsp;
with its blend of high-octane action and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:10.160
chilling horror. But what has the cast been up&nbsp;
to in the two decades since the film's release?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:12.960
We're here to catch you upon the&nbsp;
goings-on of The Mummy's cast,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:15.920
from the Oscars they've won to&nbsp;
the challenges they've faced.

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:20.800
Brendan Fraser plays the lead role of Rick&nbsp;
O’Connell, a rugged adventurer who leads an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:25.680
expedition to Hamunaptra , the city of the dead&nbsp;
where the high priest Imhotep’s corpse resides.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:29.360
When it turns out that the terrifying&nbsp;
legends about this mysterious city are true,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:31.440
his travels take a deadly turn.

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:36.080
Initially, Fraser found continued success in&nbsp;
the sequels The Mummy Returns, and The Mummy:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:41.120
Tomb of the Dragon Emperor. He also starred&nbsp;
in a remake of the 1967 film Bedazzled,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:44.800
Looney Tunes: Back in Action,&nbsp;
and the Oscar-winning film Crash.

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:50.560
However, after being assaulted in 2003, losing&nbsp;
his mother, and going through a bitter divorce,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:53.520
the star took it upon himself&nbsp;
to leave Hollywood behind.

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:55.280
Fraser told GQ Magazine:

00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:58.240
“I bought into the pressure that comes&nbsp;
[…] with a professional life that’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:02.640
being molded and shaped and guided and&nbsp;
managed. That requires what they call a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:07.440
thick skin. […] I just felt I couldn’t be a&nbsp;
part of it. I didn’t feel that I belonged.”

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:11.040
In recent years though, Fraser has&nbsp;
made a modest return to the industry.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:14.400
You may have spotted him in&nbsp;
series such as Trust, Condor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:19.680
or Doom Patrol, where he provides his own&nbsp;
idiosyncratic take on the DC Comics hero Robotman.

00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:26.480
After reading aloud from the ancient Book of&nbsp;
the Dead, librarian and aspiring Egyptologist&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:30.800
Evelyn Carnahan unintentionally wakes&nbsp;
up Imhotep from his eternal slumber.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:34.000
Played by Rachel Weisz , Carnahan&nbsp;
must fight to survive as the undead&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:38.720
high priest strives to sacrifice her in&nbsp;
order to resurrect his long-dead lover.

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:43.280
Following the success of The Mummy and The Mummy&nbsp;
Returns, Weisz went on to build an impressive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.280 --> 00:01:48.000
film career for herself. In addition to winning&nbsp;
an Oscar for her role in The Constant Gardener,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:52.160
she also starred in numerous other highly&nbsp;
regarded films, such as The Lobster,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.160 --> 00:01:55.040
The Favourite, and The Light Between Oceans.

00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:57.280
Her personal life has been just as busy.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.280 --> 00:02:00.160
After spending a number of years&nbsp;
being married to renowned director&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.160 --> 00:02:04.320
Darren Aronofsky , she got hitched to&nbsp;
Daniel Craig and became a mother of two.

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:09.760
John Hannah plays Evelyn’s brother, Jonathan&nbsp;
Carnahan, who sets the story in motion by giving&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.760 --> 00:02:14.240
her a map to Hamunaptra. After confessing that he&nbsp;
stole it from Rick, who has since been imprisoned,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.240 --> 00:02:18.560
the two set off to free him and enlist him to&nbsp;
travel with them to the ancient city of the dead.

00:02:18.560 --> 00:02:22.240
After starring in The Mummy trilogy,&nbsp;
Hannah focused more on television,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:25.520
where he became a regular on&nbsp;
numerous series, including Carnivale,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.520 --> 00:02:30.160
Trust Me, and Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D. However,&nbsp;
he made appearances in a few films as well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:35.840
The Hurricane and Ghost Son being two that&nbsp;
he has claimed to be particularly fond of.

00:02:35.840 --> 00:02:38.400
His newest endeavors include the sci-fi comedy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:42.640
The Intergalactic Adventures of Max&nbsp;
Cloud, and The Auschwitz Report.

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:49.440
Patricia Velasquez plays Anck-su-namun , Imhotep’s&nbsp;
illicit lover and Pharaoh Seti’s mistress.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:53.360
After having an affair behind the Pharaoh's&nbsp;
back, and subsequently killing him in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.360 --> 00:02:58.858
order to keep their secret, they both face&nbsp;
fatal consequences that echo through time.

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:08.960
Velasquez has continued her&nbsp;
acting career since The Mummy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.960 --> 00:03:14.480
starring in TV series like Arrested Development,&nbsp;
American Family, and the L Word. She also played&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:18.080
the role of Patricia Alvarez in the&nbsp;
horror film The Curse of La Llorona .

00:03:18.080 --> 00:03:23.120
Outside of Hollywood, Velasquez is also a&nbsp;
committed activist. In 2002, she founded the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.120 --> 00:03:27.840
Wayuu Taya Foundation, which works to support&nbsp;
indigenous communities in Latin America.

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:32.080
She also published an autobiography,&nbsp;
Straight Walk, in 2015,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.080 --> 00:03:34.800
in which she officially came out as a lesbian.

00:03:34.800 --> 00:03:36.240
In the book, she writes:

00:03:36.240 --> 00:03:40.160
“As my daughter started growing up and I&nbsp;
was teaching her to be honest and proud,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:44.080
I knew it was time for me to set an&nbsp;
example — which meant facing my truth.”

00:03:46.146 --> 00:03:50.320
Arnold Vosloo plays the memorable and&nbsp;
terrifying Imhotep, who not only wipes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.320 --> 00:03:55.280
out a group of treasure hunters, but also&nbsp;
brings back the ten plagues of ancient Egypt.

00:03:55.280 --> 00:03:59.200
Though he starred in the sequel, The Mummy&nbsp;
Returns, he did not reprise his role in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:03.040
the final installment of the trilogy,&nbsp;
Tomb of the Dragon Emperor. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.040 --> 00:04:08.320
he did go on to act in many other films&nbsp;
and TV series, including 24, G.I. Joe:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.320 --> 00:04:14.080
The Rise of Cobra, G.I. Joe: Retaliation,&nbsp;
Blood Diamond, and Tom Clancy’s Jack Ryan.

00:04:14.080 --> 00:04:17.280
He is also a prolific voice&nbsp;
actor, having appeared in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.280 --> 00:04:21.200
everything from All-Star Superman&nbsp;
to Voltron: Legendary Defender.

00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:26.800
Jonathan Hyde plays Dr. Allen Chamberlain, who&nbsp;
hopes to strike it rich on his expedition to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.800 --> 00:04:29.840
Egypt. Traveling with a group&nbsp;
of treasure hunters to Cairo,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.840 --> 00:04:33.520
he opens a chest that contains the&nbsp;
Book of the Dead. Because of this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.520 --> 00:04:38.240
he is marked with the curse of Imhotep,&nbsp;
who consumes his life energy, killing him.

00:04:38.240 --> 00:04:42.800
Since The Mummy, he has appeared in films&nbsp;
such as Land of the Blind and Crimson Peak,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:46.800
and TV series such as The Strain&nbsp;
and Trollhunters: Tales of Arcadia.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.800 --> 00:04:52.960
He also has many theatre accolades, including&nbsp;
roles in King Lear, Peter Pan, and Julias Caesar.

00:04:52.960 --> 00:04:55.680
His most recent theater work was&nbsp;
his performance as Richard Nixon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.680 --> 00:04:58.480
in Frost/Nixon at the Sheffield Crucible Theater.

00:05:00.540 --> 00:05:03.920
Kevin J. O’Connor plays Beni Gabor , a&nbsp;
selfish treasure hunter who’s willing to use&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.920 --> 00:05:08.800
anyone in order to come out on top. This mindset&nbsp;
leads him to swear his devotion to Imhotep,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.800 --> 00:05:12.240
and ultimately ends up&nbsp;
ensuring his untimely demise.

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:17.120
Besides playing Beni, O’Connor is likely best&nbsp;
known for his roles as Igor in Van Helsing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:17.120 --> 00:05:23.200
and Henry in There Will Be Blood. He’s also been&nbsp;
involved in the Stephen King mini-series 11.22.63,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.200 --> 00:05:28.720
the television adaptation of Joseph Heller’s Catch&nbsp;
22, and On Becoming a God in Central Florida.

00:05:29.440 --> 00:05:30.080
Oded Fehr

00:05:30.080 --> 00:05:34.080
Oded Fehr plays the fierce warrior, Ardeth&nbsp;
Bay, who leads the Medjai in Hamunaptra.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.080 --> 00:05:38.640
The Medjai are descendants of Pharaoh Seti’s&nbsp;
palace guards, who guard Imhotep’s tomb.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.640 --> 00:05:42.560
Though Ardeth warns the explorers to leave,&nbsp;
they choose not to heed his warnings.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:42.560 --> 00:05:46.560
Consequently, they must turn to him&nbsp;
for help after Imhotep is resurrected.

00:05:46.560 --> 00:05:47.760
[The Mummy 01:41:57 - Ardeth cocks his shotgun]

00:05:47.760 --> 00:05:52.240
In addition to The Mummy, Fehr has starred&nbsp;
in Deuce Bigalow: Male Gigolo, and three&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:52.240 --> 00:05:58.240
Resident Evil movies — specifically Apocalypse,&nbsp;
Extinction, and Retribution. He has also landed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.240 --> 00:06:04.080
regular roles in several series including The&nbsp;
First, When Heroes Fly, and Once Upon a Time.

00:06:04.080 --> 00:06:08.160
He married producer Rhonda Tollefson in&nbsp;
2000, and has three children with her.

00:06:09.200 --> 00:06:11.600
Erick Avari plays Dr. Terrence Bey,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:11.600 --> 00:06:16.000
Evelyn’s boss and curator of the Cairo&nbsp;
Museum of Antiquities. Later in the film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:20.880
we find out that he's actually working with the&nbsp;
Medjai to prevent Imhotep from being resurrected.

00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:25.920
You may otherwise know him best as Cecil&nbsp;
Anderson in the 2002 comedy, Mr. Deeds,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.920 --> 00:06:31.120
or as Tival in the 2001 remake of Planet of&nbsp;
the Apes. He's also taken on roles in numerous&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:31.120 --> 00:06:37.840
TV series, such as Heroes, The Middleman,&nbsp;
Leverage, Hung, The Brink, and The Chosen.

00:06:37.840 --> 00:06:43.520
In 2015, he made his directorial debut with the&nbsp;
film, Chasing Eagle Rock. He’s even worked as a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:43.520 --> 00:06:48.480
voice actor, most prominently portraying Master&nbsp;
Rahool in the Destiny series of video games.

00:06:49.520 --> 00:06:53.200
Stephen Dunham plays Dr. Henderson,&nbsp;
a gentleman who tags along with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:53.200 --> 00:06:57.120
treasure hunters in hopes of becoming&nbsp;
rich. As we've already recalled,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:57.120 --> 00:07:01.680
things don't end well for them after they open&nbsp;
the chest that contains the Book of the Dead.

00:07:01.680 --> 00:07:07.200
His most prominent work besides The Mummy was&nbsp;
his supporting role in the 2008 comedy Get Smart,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:07.200 --> 00:07:10.160
and for playing Dr. Chamberlain in Monster-in-Law.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:10.160 --> 00:07:14.400
He also acted in TV series&nbsp;
such as DAG and Oh, Grow Up.

00:07:14.400 --> 00:07:18.320
His role in Paranormal Activity 4&nbsp;
ended up being his last acting gig,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.320 --> 00:07:21.600
as he sadly passed away from a&nbsp;
heart attack at the age of 48.

00:07:23.520 --> 00:07:27.760
Corey Johnson plays Mr. Daniels, another member&nbsp;
of the ill-fated treasure hunting troupe.

00:07:27.760 --> 00:07:33.520
Despite his swift end in The Mummy, he's&nbsp;
consistently proved his staying power as an actor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:33.520 --> 00:07:37.760
with roles in blockbusters such as The&nbsp;
Bourne Ultimatum, Captain Phillips,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.760 --> 00:07:43.040
and Ex Machina. Like numerous others in&nbsp;
The Mummy cast, he has dabbled in theater.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:43.040 --> 00:07:48.080
His most notable accolade is his performance&nbsp;
as Mitch in A Streetcar Named Desire.

00:07:48.080 --> 00:07:52.240
Johnson's newest endeavors include roles&nbsp;
in the short film Swept Under the Rug,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:52.240 --> 00:07:54.480
and the full-length feature Morbius.

00:07:55.600 --> 00:08:00.000
Lastly, Tuc Watkins plays Mr. Burns —&nbsp;
another member of the treasure hunter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:04.480
troupe who fails to escape the curse of&nbsp;
Imhotep once the ancient chest is opened.

00:08:04.480 --> 00:08:08.160
He's best known for his role as&nbsp;
David Vickers on the soap opera,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:08.160 --> 00:08:11.840
One Life to Live, and also his role&nbsp;
as Bob Hunter on Desperate Housewives.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:12.400 --> 00:08:16.560
If that’s not your cup of tea, you can find him&nbsp;
on the mystery web series Where the Bears Are,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:16.560 --> 00:08:19.920
or on the second season of the&nbsp;
dark comedy series Black Monday.

00:08:19.920 --> 00:08:22.960
In 2013, he came out as&nbsp;
gay on an episode of Marie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.960 --> 00:08:26.240
and announced that he'd become the&nbsp;
father of twins, via a surrogate.

00:08:26.240 --> 00:08:28.800
He recalled his thoughts when he was much younger:

00:08:28.800 --> 00:08:32.160
“I knew I was gay, and I knew&nbsp;
one day I was going to be a dad.”

00:08:32.160 --> 00:08:37.920
Though The Mummy was released to mixed reviews&nbsp;
in 1999, it has surely become a movie that all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:37.920 --> 00:08:43.200
of us remember fondly. It was the epitome of a&nbsp;
summer blockbuster: incredible action sequences,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:43.200 --> 00:08:48.560
spooky curses, and the triumph of good over&nbsp;
evil. But beyond just being a fun movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:48.560 --> 00:08:51.520
The Mummy helped pave the way for&nbsp;
many subsequent action movies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:51.520 --> 00:08:55.840
while simultaneously taking cues from&nbsp;
the much older films that influenced it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:55.840 --> 00:09:01.040
It’s a classic, and we have no doubt that it&nbsp;
will continue to be for many years to come.

